        ],
        "text" => "(W regexp) (only under C<S<use feature 'enhanced_xx'>>)\nYour pattern contains an unescaped C<#> character which causes it and\nall text up through the end of the current line to be considered a\ncomment.  The normal style for such comments is for the C<#> to be\nsurrounded by at least one white space character on each side.  And this\nwasn't.  That makes it look like it might have been intended to be taken\nas a literal C<#> character.  This warning is intended to alert you to\nthe possibility that your pattern won't behave as you intended.\nIf the C<#> is intended to taken literally, change it to C<\\#>.\nIf it was intended to start a comment, change it to S<C< # >>.\n\n"
