        "text" => "(W regexp) (only under C<S<use feature 'enhanced_xx'>>)\nYour pattern contains a bracketed character class with a comment, and\ninside that comment is an unescaped, unquoted C<]> character, which\nnormally is used to terminate the character class.  Thus the class isn't\nterminated here, but goes on to include other lines.  This warning is\nintended to catch cases where that isn't what was intended.  If the C<]>\nis intended to be part of the comment, quote or escape it suppress the\nmessage.  If it was intended to terminate the class, simply make it to\nbe on a new line in the source code.\n\n"
